{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git log -1 --format=%s && rg -n \\\"constraint|0\\\\.14|0\\\\.06|30°\\\" reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/palette*prompt* docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md | head -80 && cat package.json\"","aggregated_output":"Default palette for both schemes, fitted to the A5 thresholds (candidate, not reviewed)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/palette.review.prompt.md:12:2. **Do the thresholds mean what the spec says?** For each of the six constraints in the tests: is the quantity tested the one A5 names; is the threshold on the scale A5 uses; is \"worst case over deficiencies\" computed over the right set; are translucent fills composited in the right space over the right background. Is any constraint vacuous or weaker than stated (for example a difference measured after rounding to 8 bits, or a hue comparison that wraps wrongly at 360°)?\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/palette.review.prompt.md:14:4. **Are the tests able to fail?** For each test, name a palette change that violates the stated rule and check the test catches it. Are expected thresholds taken from the spec or tuned to the result (the author says most constraints sit within 5% of the limit)?\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/palette.review.prompt.md:15:5. **The feasibility claims.** The author says the lightness spread (three deep colours on white; a medium-dark first blue in the dark scheme) is forced by the constraints, and that relaxing two thresholds to 0.08 and 0.12 did not help. Is the search exhaustive over what it claims (grid resolution, bounds, pruning soundness in the branch and bound)? Can you exhibit a palette that meets all six constraints with a visibly more even lightness, or show why none exists at this grid? If the simulation model or severity is stricter than A5 requires, say so: that would be the cheapest way to a better-looking palette.\n{\n  \"name\": \"axylo-workspace\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"workspaces\": [\n    \"packages/*\"\n  ],\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc -p packages/axylo --noEmit && tsc -p docs/api && tsc -p packages/react\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\",\n    \"build\": \"node scripts/build.mjs\",\n    \"size\": \"node scripts/size.mjs\",\n    \"test:browser\": \"AXYLO_BROWSER=1 vitest run\",\n    \"check\": \"npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run build && npm run test:browser && npm run size\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/node\": \"^26.6.6\",\n    \"@types/react\": \"^19.3.0\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"^19.3.0\",\n    \"axe-core\": \"^4.14.1\",\n    \"esbuild\": \"^0.28.2\",\n    \"fast-check\": \"^4.10.2\",\n    \"playwright-core\": \"^1.65.1\",\n    \"react\": \"^19.3.1\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"^19.3.1\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^7.0.2\",\n    \"vitest\": \"^5.1.0\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
