{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show 51e1be5:packages/axylo/src/dom/swatch.ts | head -67 && git grep -n \\\"seriesSwatch\\\" 51e1be5 -- packages/axylo/src && git show 51e1be5:docs/02-product-spec.md | sed -n '198,213p' && git log --oneline -7\"","aggregated_output":"/**\n * The legend and tooltip swatch: a small SVG that repeats how a series is drawn (spec A5): a filled square\n * for bars and areas (with the bar's pattern past the eighth series, spec F9), the line with its dash and\n * marker for lines, the marker for scatter. The color is the series' custom property on the chart root\n * (`--axylo-series-color-N`), so a theme change or forced colors restyle it with no call.\n *\n * A hidden series is drawn as an outline of the same shape (spec I2: marked by shape, not by dimming).\n */\nimport type { MarkerShape, SeriesCue } from '../core/contracts';\nimport { MARKER_POLYGONS } from '../render/geometry';\n\nconst NS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';\n\nexport interface SwatchSpec {\n  /** Palette index of the series (or slice), null for a muted entry such as a donut's \"Other\". */\n  readonly color: number | null;\n  readonly cue: SeriesCue | null;\n  /** Draw the short dashed stroke of a line behind the marker. */\n  readonly line: boolean;\n  /** Outline only: the series is hidden. */\n  readonly hollow: boolean;\n  /** A filled square whatever the marker (bars and areas fill a region, they have no marker). */\n  readonly fill?: boolean;\n  /** The bar pattern drawn over the fill in the background color, or null. */\n  readonly pattern?: 'diagonal' | 'cross' | 'dots' | null;\n}\n\nconst BACKGROUND = 'var(--axylo-background, var(--axylo-backdrop, var(--axylo-default-background)))';\n\n/** The pattern inside the 10 × 10 chip at (5, 1), as path data: lines x + y = c (and x − y = c), or dots. */\nfunction patternPath(kind: 'diagonal' | 'cross' | 'dots'): string {\n  const x0 = 5, y0 = 1, size = 10;\n  if (kind === 'dots') {\n    let d = '';\n    for (const [cx, cy] of [[7.5, 3.5], [12.5, 3.5], [10, 6], [7.5, 8.5], [12.5, 8.5]] as const) {\n      d += `M${cx + 1} ${cy}a1 1 0 1 0 -2 0a1 1 0 1 0 2 0Z`;\n    }\n    return d;\n  }\n  let d = '';\n  // Diagonals every 4 px, clipped to the chip by hand (no <clipPath>, so no ids to keep unique).\n  for (let c = 4; c < 2 * size; c += 4) {\n    const a = Math.max(0, c - size);\n    const b = Math.min(size, c);\n    d += `M${x0 + a} ${y0 + size - (c - a)}L${x0 + b} ${y0 + size - (c - b)}`;\n    if (kind === 'cross') d += `M${x0 + a} ${y0 + (c - a)}L${x0 + b} ${y0 + (c - b)}`;\n  }\n  return d;\n}\n\nfunction colorOf(index: number | null): string {\n  return index === null ? 'var(--axylo-muted, var(--axylo-default-muted))' : `var(--axylo-series-color-${index + 1})`;\n}\n\nfunction markerPath(shape: MarkerShape, cx: number, cy: number, size: number): string {\n  if (shape === 'circle') {\n    const r = size / 2;\n    return `M${cx - r} ${cy}a${r} ${r} 0 1 0 ${2 * r} 0a${r} ${r} 0 1 0 ${-2 * r} 0Z`;\n  }\n  const poly = MARKER_POLYGONS[shape];\n  let d = '';\n  for (let k = 0; k < poly.length; k += 2) {\n    d += `${k === 0 ? 'M' : 'L'}${(cx + poly[k]! * size).toFixed(2)} ${(cy + poly[k + 1]! * size).toFixed(2)}`;\n  }\n  return d + 'Z';\n}\n\n51e1be5:packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:111:export function seriesSwatch(kind: ControlsState['kind'], index: number, cue: SwatchSpec['cue'], hollow: boolean): SwatchSpec {\n51e1be5:packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:288:      return seriesSwatch(view.kind, row.seriesIndex, view.cues[row.seriesIndex] ?? null, false);\n51e1be5:packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:860:        struck: !shown, swatch: seriesSwatch(view.kind, i, view.cues[i] ?? null, !shown),\n| Reference lines and bands | Yes; included in the domain; listed in the summary and table caption | Yes | Yes | No | Yes |\n\n### 3.7 Compact variant\n\n`compact: true` on line, area and bar draws the marks and nothing else: no axes, gridlines, legend, toolbar, table control, zoom or tooltip. It is for a small tile where the page already shows the number and the label.\n\n| ID | Criterion | Verified by |\n|---|---|---|\n| C1 | A compact chart is a static image with a full text alternative: `role=\"img\"`, an accessible name (as in A1, including AX140 when none is given) and the generated summary as its description (series, x range, minimum, maximum, last value, omissions). It has no tab stop and no pointer-only behavior, so nothing is available to a mouse that is not available to a keyboard. | Accessibility-tree snapshot; a page of 40 has zero added tab stops |\n| C2 | The fidelity rules still hold: zero baseline for bar and area (F1), gaps (F2), diagnostics (F3), simplified drawing (F5), sorting (F11), no motion (I5), scheme from the page (L4). | The same fixtures as the full charts |\n| C3 | It fills its container at any size from 24×16 CSS px up; with no definite height it is 32 px tall. | Size tests |\n| C4 | With more than one series, lines differ by dash as well as color, since there is no legend; AX131 suggests one series per compact chart. | Two-series fixture |\n| C5 | When values were left out (F12), the description says so and a small marker with a text equivalent appears in the corner. | `dirty` fixture in compact mode |\n\nA compact chart does not give access to every value; the summary is its alternative. An author who needs every value reachable uses the full chart.\n\n51e1be5 Default palette for both schemes, fitted to the A5 thresholds (candidate, not reviewed)\nba4e572 Status: core fix pass and React fixes committed; second core fix pass, palette and harness fixes running\n156f414 Chart core: the 20 findings of the first core review fixed; SVG default; legend positions\na63bbee React adapter: review fixes (14 findings) and a real build\n6bd5f9c Acceptance matrix as data with a checker (Codex gpt-6.2-sol xhigh)\n5522583 Benchmark review recorded (Codex gpt-6.2-sol max: 5 blocking, 12 major, 1 minor); decision 0002 made provisional\n1cafb11 Review of the React adapter by Codex gpt-6.2-astra xhigh recorded (1 blocking, 7 major, 6 minor)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
